# API & Service Patterns

## Axios Instance (`lib/api/axios.ts`)

- Base URL: `/api/v1` (from `config/constants.ts`).
- `withCredentials: true` for httpOnly refresh cookies.
- Request interceptor injects `Bearer <token>` from auth state.
- Response interceptor catches 401, refreshes token, retries once.
- All API calls go through this instance. Never use raw `fetch()`.

## Standard Response Envelope (`types/api.ts`)

Backend responses follow `ServiceResponse<T>`:
```typescript
{ data: T, success: boolean, message: string }
```
Paginated endpoints return `PaginatedResponse<T>` wrapping `PaginatedData<T>`.

## Query / Mutation Wrapper Hooks (`lib/api/`)

ALWAYS use `useDataQuery` and `useDataMutation` from `@/lib/api/`. Never call `useQuery` / `useMutation` directly in services.

### `useDataQuery<T>(queryKey, fnOrUrl, options?)`

- `fnOrUrl` can be a GET endpoint string (`"/users"`) or an async function returning `T`.
- String shorthand auto-calls `api.get<T>(url)`.
- Typed error is always `AppAxiosError`.

### `useDataMutation<TData, TVariables>(mutationFn, options?)`

- `invalidateKeys` -- query keys to invalidate on success.
- `successMessage` / `errorMessage` -- auto-toasts via NotificationProvider. Pass `false` to suppress.
- Error message auto-extracted from `AppAxiosError` response body.

## Service File Pattern

```typescript
// features/<name>/services/<name>Service.ts
import { useDataQuery } from "@/lib/api/useDataQuery.ts";
import { useDataMutation } from "@/lib/api/useDataMutation.ts";
import api from "@/lib/api/axios.ts";
import type { Item, CreateItemPayload } from "../interfaces/<name>.interfaces.ts";

// Raw API functions (pure, no hooks)
async function fetchItems(): Promise<Item[]> {
  return (await api.get<Item[]>("/items")).data;
}
async function createItem(payload: CreateItemPayload): Promise<Item> {
  return (await api.post<Item>("/items", payload)).data;
}

// Hook exports (what pages/components consume)
export const useItems = () =>
  useDataQuery<Item[]>(["items"], fetchItems, { staleTime: 60_000 });

export const useCreateItem = () =>
  useDataMutation<Item, CreateItemPayload>(createItem, {
    invalidateKeys: [["items"]],
    successMessage: "Item created",
  });
```

## Rules

- Query keys: `["feature", "resource", ...params]` hierarchy.
- Error extraction: use `extractErrorMessage()` from `@/lib/api/types.ts`.
- Type every response generically: `api.get<MyType>(url)`.
- Never put TanStack Query hooks in `hooks/`. Global hooks are only for context consumers. Query hooks belong in the feature's `services/`.
